{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:03:09.002141336Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arecipe-tooling-0eaee18fe59bc3d7","agent_type":"recipe-tooling","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"git diff --numstat main..HEAD -- Makefile cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd.go cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd_test.go cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd.go cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd_test.go examples/recipes/README.md"},"tool_input_hash":"48763392f7b61cb4b8a56626b47d331adb9067f8969352187f8fd27acce0d2b7","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"git diff --numstat main..HEAD -- Makefile cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd.go cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd_test.go cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd.go cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd_test.go examples/rec..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:03:11.000986773Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# verify-recipe-path.sh -- drive beadle-daemon's recipe tooling end to end.\n#\n# Proves the operator-facing path works: mint a key, init daemon.json, sign a\n# recipe, detect tampering, and (when the subcommand exists) verify a signature\n# without starting the daemon.\n#\n# Runs entirely inside a scratch HOME and GNUPGHOME. It never touches\n# ~/.punt-labs/beadle or the real keyring.\n#\n# Two deliberate choices worth knowing before editing:\n#\n#  1. Exit codes are captured directly, never through a pipe. Running a command\n#     under test through `| tail` yields tail's status, not the command's --\n#     which silently reported a FAILING command as exit 0 the first time this\n#     sequence was run by hand.\n#  2. GNUPGHOME lives under /tmp/bg-* rather than the repo's .tmp/. gpg-agent\n#     opens a Unix socket there and the path limit is 108 bytes; the deep .tmp\n#     path overflows it. Same rule docs/TESTING.md states for the Go tests.\n\nset -uo pipefail\n\nreadonly REPO=\"${REPO:-$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)}\"\nreadonly DAEMON=\"$REPO/beadle-daemon\"\nreadonly RECIPE_SRC=\"$REPO/examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml\"\n\npass=0\nfail=0\nskip=0\n\nscratch=\"\"\ncleanup() {\n  [[ -n \"$scratch\" \u0026\u0026 -d \"$scratch\" ]] || return 0\n  # gpg-agent holds the socket; stop it before removing its home.\n  GNUPGHOME=\"$scratch/gpg\" gpgconf --kill gpg-agent \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || true\n  chmod -R u+w \"$scratch\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true\n  rm -rf \"$scratch\"\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\n\nok()      { printf '  \\033[32mPASS\\033[0m  %s\\n' \"$1\"; pass=$((pass + 1)); }\nbad()     { printf '  \\033[31mFAIL\\033[0m  %s\\n' \"$1\"; fail=$((fail + 1)); }\nskipped() { printf '  \\033[33mSKIP\\033[0m  %s\\n' \"$1\"; skip=$((skip + 1)); }\nhead2()   { printf '\\n\\033[1m%s\\033[0m\\n' \"$1\"; }\n\n# check \u003clabel\u003e \u003cexpected-exit\u003e \u003ccmd...\u003e\n# Captures status directly. Stores combined output in $out for the caller.\nout=\"\"\ncheck() {\n  local label=\"$1\" want=\"$2\"; shift 2\n  out=$(\"$@\" 2\u003e\u00261)\n  local rc=$?\n  if [[ \"$rc\" -eq \"$want\" ]]; then\n    ok \"$label (exit $rc)\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  bad \"$label -- wanted exit $want, got $rc\"\n  printf '        %s\\n' \"${out:0:300}\"\n  return 1\n}\n\n# --- preflight -------------------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"Preflight\"\n\nif [[ ! -x \"$DAEMON\" ]]; then\n  printf '  beadle-daemon not built. Run: make build-daemon\\n'\n  exit 2\nfi\nok \"beadle-daemon present ($(\"$DAEMON\" version 2\u003e/dev/null | head -1))\"\n\nif [[ ! -f \"$RECIPE_SRC\" ]]; then\n  printf '  missing %s\\n' \"$RECIPE_SRC\"\n  exit 2\nfi\nok \"example recipe present\"\n\ncommand -v gpg \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || { printf '  gpg not on PATH\\n'; exit 2; }\nok \"gpg present ($(gpg --version | head -1))\"\n\n# --- isolated environment --------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"Isolating environment\"\n\nscratch=$(mktemp -d /tmp/bg-recipe-XXXXXX) || exit 2\nexport GNUPGHOME=\"$scratch/gpg\"\nexport HOME=\"$scratch/home\"\nmkdir -p \"$GNUPGHOME\" \"$HOME\"\nchmod 700 \"$GNUPGHOME\"\nok \"scratch HOME and GNUPGHOME under $scratch\"\n\n# An unprotected key: the configuration `sign` works with today.\ngpg --batch --passphrase '' --quick-generate-key \\\n    \"Recipe Open \u003c[redacted-email]\u003e\" ed25519 sign 1y \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\nFPR_OPEN=$(gpg --list-keys --with-colons [redacted-email] 2\u003e/dev/null |\n           awk -F: '/^fpr:/{print $10; exit}')\n[[ -n \"$FPR_OPEN\" ]] \u0026\u0026 ok \"minted unprotected key ${FPR_OPEN:0:16}...\" \\\n                     || bad \"could not mint unprotected key\"\n\n# A passphrase-protected key: what a real authorizer key should look like.\ngpg --batch --passphrase 'correct horse battery staple' --quick-generate-key \\\n    \"Recipe Locked \u003c[redacted-email]\u003e\" ed25519 sign 1y \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\nFPR_LOCKED=$(gpg --list-keys --with-colons [redacted-email] 2\u003e/dev/null |\n             awk -F: '/^fpr:/{print $10; exit}')\n[[ -n \"$FPR_LOCKED\" ]] \u0026\u0026 ok \"minted protected key ${FPR_LOCKED:0:16}...\" \\\n                       || bad \"could not mint protected key\"\n\n# --- init ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"init\"\n\nCONF=\"$HOME/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json\"\n\ncheck \"init writes daemon.json\" 0 \"$DAEMON\" init --fingerprint \"$FPR_OPEN\"\n\nif [[ -f \"$CONF\" ]] \u0026\u0026 grep -q \"$FPR_OPEN\" \"$CONF\"; then\n  ok \"daemon.json names the authorizer key\"\nelse\n  bad \"daemon.json missing or wrong key\"\nfi\n\nif [[ -f \"$CONF\" ]]; then\n  perm=$(stat -c '%a' \"$CONF\" 2\u003e/dev/null || stat -f '%Lp' \"$CONF\" 2\u003e/dev/null)\n  # Config names a key id, not a secret, but it governs trust -- world-writable\n  # would let any local user redirect which key authorizes recipes.\n  case \"$perm\" in\n    6??|7??) ok \"daemon.json not group/world writable ($perm)\" ;;\n    *)       bad \"daemon.json permissions are $perm\" ;;\n  esac\nfi\n\ncheck \"second init refuses to clobber\" 1 \"$DAEMON\" init --fingerprint \"$FPR_OPEN\"\n[[ \"$out\" == *--force* ]] \u0026\u0026 ok \"refusal names --force as the remedy\" \\\n                          || bad \"refusal does not mention --force\"\n\ncheck \"init --force overwrites\" 0 \"$DAEMON\" init --fingerprint \"$FPR_OPEN\" --force\n\n# --- sign ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"sign\"\n\nR1=\"$scratch/unsigned.yaml\"\ncp \"$RECIPE_SRC\" \"$R1\"\n\nif grep -q \"BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE\" \"$R1\"; then\n  bad \"example recipe ships pre-signed -- it should not\"\nelse\n  ok \"example recipe ships unsigned\"\nfi\n\ncheck \"sign an unsigned recipe\" 0 \"$DAEMON\" sign \"$R1\" --signer \"$FPR_OPEN\"\ngrep -q \"BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE\" \"$R1\" \u0026\u0026 ok \"signature written into the file\" \\\n                                    || bad \"no signature in the file\"\n# The tool must prove its own output verifies; a signing tool that emits an\n# unverifiable signature is worse than none.\n[[ \"$out\" == *round-trip* || \"$out\" == *verif* ]] \\\n  \u0026\u0026 ok \"sign reports its round-trip verification\" \\\n  || bad \"sign does not report a round-trip check\"\n\nR2=\"$scratch/tampered.yaml\"\ncp \"$R1\" \"$R2\"\nsed -i.bak 's/^description:.*/description: TAMPERED AFTER SIGNING/' \"$R2\" 2\u003e/dev/null \\\n  || sed -i '' 's/^description:.*/description: TAMPERED AFTER SIGNING/' \"$R2\"\nrm -f \"$R2.bak\"\n\n# --- verify ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"verify\"\n\nif \"$DAEMON\" verify --help \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then\n  check \"verify accepts a validly signed recipe\" 0 \"$DAEMON\" verify \"$R1\"\n  check \"verify rejects a tampered recipe\" 1 \"$DAEMON\" verify \"$R2\"\n  check \"verify rejects an unsigned recipe\" 1 \"$DAEMON\" verify \"$RECIPE_SRC\"\nelse\n  skipped \"no 'verify' subcommand yet -- an operator cannot check a signature\"\n  skipped \"  without starting the daemon and reading its logs (round-2 item)\"\nfi\n\n# --- protected key ---------------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"Protected signing key\"\n\nR3=\"$scratch/locked.yaml\"\ncp \"$RECIPE_SRC\" \"$R3\"\nout=$(\"$DAEMON\" sign \"$R3\" --signer \"$FPR_LOCKED\" 2\u003e\u00261)\nrc=$?\n\nif [[ \"$rc\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n  ok \"signed with a passphrase-protected key (passphrase resolved)\"\nelif [[ \"$out\" == *gpg-passphrase* || \"$out\" == *BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE* ]]; then\n  # Failing is fine with no credential stored. Failing WITHOUT naming the\n  # credential is the defect: a real authorizer key should be protected, so a\n  # message that does not point at the fix steers operators toward an\n  # unprotected signing key.\n  ok \"failure names the gpg-passphrase credential as the fix\"\nelse\n  bad \"failure gives no path forward (round-2 item)\"\n  printf '        %s\\n' \"${out:0:200}\"\nfi\n\n# --- summary ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\nhead2 \"Summary\"\nprintf '  %d passed, %d failed, %d skipped\\n\\n' \"$pass\" \"$fail\" \"$skip\"\n[[ \"$fail\" -eq 0 ]] || exit 1\n","file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/verify-recipe-path.sh"},"tool_input_hash":"da838e66fe3c83956ff493a0d7c7105b1d1a666562eb1a45c21ef244f0954a5d","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# verify-recipe-path.sh -- drive beadle-daemon's recipe tooling end to end.\\n#\\n# Proves the operator-facing path works: mint a key, init daemon.json, sign a\\n# recipe...","redacted":true}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:03:25.529509852Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; ls .bin/ | head -20; echo \"=== safety lib API ===\"; grep -nE \"^[a-z_]+\\(\\)|^# \" .bin/lib/safety.sh 2\u003e/dev/null | head -30","description":"Read .bin conventions and safety library"},"tool_input_hash":"2f486f2dfffbd57a3b3e2d6947f67b3878c2c047b3b2904804edd37aa2632acd","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; ls .bin/ | head -20; echo \\\"=== safety lib API ===\\\"; grep -nE \\\"^[a-z_]+\\\\(\\\\)|^# \\\" .bin/lib/safety.sh 2\\u003e/dev/null | head -30\",\"description\":\"Read .bin conven..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:03:34.704564918Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arecipe-tooling-0eaee18fe59bc3d7","agent_type":"recipe-tooling","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"mission: m-2026-08-31-005\nround: 2\nauthor: bwk\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.92\nfiles_changed:\n  - path: Makefile\n    added: 15\n    removed: 7\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd.go\n    added: 144\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd_test.go\n    added: 189\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd.go\n    added: 121\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd_test.go\n    added: 128\n    removed: 0\n  - path: examples/recipes/README.md\n    added: 100\n    removed: 0\nevidence:\n  - name: make check (shellcheck now sweeps scripts/beadle-sysreport, vet, staticcheck, golangci-lint 0 issues, govulncheck 0 findings, markdownlint 0 errors, go test -race -count=1 ./... all green)\n    status: pass\n  - name: make lint-shell — confirmed scripts/beadle-sysreport now appears in the shellcheck invocation list, and only that one file was added versus the old *.sh glob (comm -3 diff)\n    status: pass\n  - name: manual repro of the exact passphrase failure from round-1 review (real quick-generate-key with a passphrase, no --passphrase '') — confirmed the new error names the credential chain and never leaks the passphrase\n    status: pass\n  - name: manual end-to-end verify — init --fingerprint, verify on an unsigned recipe (missing), sign, verify again with no --signer (resolves from daemon.json, good)\n    status: pass\nevidence:\n  - name: go test -race -count=1 ./cmd/beadle-daemon/... — all TestRunSign_* and TestRunVerify_*/TestResolveVerifySigner_* pass, including two new real-GPG passphrase tests\n    status: pass\nprose: |\n  Three findings from round 1, all addressed.\n\n  1. PASSPHRASE ERROR (sign_cmd.go). wrapSignError wraps a\n  DetachSignBody failure only when the resolved passphrase was empty --\n  never touches the message when signing failed for some other reason\n  with a real passphrase present. The wrapped message names the\n  credential (\"gpg-passphrase\"), all three places in the resolution\n  chain (keychain, ~/.punt-labs/beadle/secrets/gpg-passphrase mode 600,\n  BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE), and states plainly that an unprotected key\n  needs none of this. It never prints the passphrase or its length --\n  the const holding the env var name had to be un-named and inlined\n  directly into the Errorf call, because gosec's G101 flagged a\n  package-level const literally named with \"Passphrase\" in it as a\n  potential hardcoded credential (false positive on the *name*, not a\n  value leak, but I did not add a suppression -- restructuring made the\n  false positive go away instead). Covered by two new tests against a\n  REAL passphrase-protected key (testenv.GenKeyWithPassphrase): one\n  proving the failure message names the fix and the passphrase never\n  appears in it, one proving BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE actually resolves\n  and signs successfully end to end -- not just that the message reads\n  right.\n\n  2. beadle-daemon verify (new files, not originally in the write set --\n  flagging this explicitly since you didn't formally amend it for these\n  two files the way you did for Makefile). Defaults to resolving the\n  authorizer key from daemon.json via a new resolveVerifySigner, which\n  mirrors main.go's resolveDaemonOwnerKeyID logic but as a plain CLI\n  error instead of a logged fail-silent-on-absence outcome (verify has\n  no reason to stay quiet about a missing daemon.json the way the\n  daemon's own startup path does). --signer overrides it for an ad-hoc\n  check against a different key. Reports the exact SignatureReason\n  (good/missing/wrong-key/key-expired/invalid) and returns a non-nil\n  error -- which cobra already turns into exit 1 -- on anything but\n  good, same as init/sign. Distinguishes an operational VerifySignature\n  failure (gpg couldn't run) from an actual signature verdict, rather\n  than reporting the former as if it were the latter. Verified by hand:\n  verify on an unsigned recipe reports \"missing\", sign it, verify again\n  with no --signer resolves from a real daemon.json and reports \"good\".\n  README.md gets a new section explaining why verify (checking against\n  daemon.json) answers a different question than sign's own round-trip\n  proof (checking against whatever --signer was passed at sign time --\n  those can differ if daemon.json's key changes later).\n\n  3. MAKEFILE GLOB (write-set amendment accepted). Replaced the *.sh\n  glob with shebang detection (word-boundary match on sh/bash/dash/zsh/\n  ksh) so an extensionless script is swept the same way a .sh one is.\n  Verified with comm -3 against the old glob's output: the only\n  difference is scripts/beadle-sysreport now included, nothing existing\n  lost or spuriously added. `make lint-shell` confirmed the new\n  invocation list, `make check` confirmed shellcheck runs it clean.\n\n  All four commits this round pass make check individually. Full\n  `make check` (shellcheck, vet, staticcheck, golangci-lint 0 issues,\n  govulncheck 0 vulnerabilities, markdownlint 0 errors, full\n  `-race` suite) is green on the whole branch, cumulative from round 1.\n","file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/missions/results/m-2026-08-31-005-round2.yaml"},"tool_input_hash":"cfe055bbb816e87c807fa4297a2ca93c6e622330873cef242e2499ef568c5e27","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"mission: m-2026-08-31-005\\nround: 2\\nauthor: bwk\\nverdict: pass\\nconfidence: 0.92\\nfiles_changed:\\n  - path: Makefile\\n    added: 15\\n    removed: 7\\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd.g..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:03:34.96295692Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; echo \"=== .bin conventions (key rules) ===\"; grep -nE \"^#{1,3} |shellcheck|set -|safety|rm -rf|destructive|dry-run\" .bin/CLAUDE.md | head -24; echo; echo \"=== pass entry present? ===\"; pass show beadle/passphrase-test-phrase \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo \"yes, readable\" || echo \"NOT readable\"","description":"Read .bin conventions and check the pass entry"},"tool_input_hash":"4d84262c5db4757015c1632dc8b4a1c70df9c1df0aea19a787c7cdb4152c353b","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; echo \\\"=== .bin conventions (key rules) ===\\\"; grep -nE \\\"^#{1,3} |shellcheck|set -|safety|rm -rf|destructive|dry-run\\\" .bin/CLAUDE.md | head -24; echo; echo \\\"=== p..."}
