{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:04:01.729905725Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arecipe-tooling-0eaee18fe59bc3d7","agent_type":"recipe-tooling","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"ethos mission advance --help 2\u003e\u00261 | head -30"},"tool_input_hash":"0c0467bf470d2c48ffe0d7e8fb0770c82fa67f3bd34518f1d129b55a73820de1","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"ethos mission advance --help 2\\u003e\\u00261 | head -30\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:04:18.911938073Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arecipe-tooling-0eaee18fe59bc3d7","agent_type":"recipe-tooling","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"All three round-2 findings are fixed and committe…","message":"All three round-2 findings are fixed and committed on feat/recipe-tooling, `make check` green (shellcheck now sweeps scripts/beadle-sysreport, golangci-lint 0 issues, govulncheck 0 vulnerabilities, markdownlint 0 errors, full -race suite).\n\n1. Passphrase error (sign_cmd.go): when the resolved passphrase is empty, the error now names the credential (\"gpg-passphrase\") and all three resolution paths (keychain, ~/.punt-labs/beadle/secrets/gpg-passphrase mode 600, BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE) — never the passphrase or its length. Reproduced your exact failure by hand and confirmed the new message; two new tests use a real passphrase-protected key (one for the failure message, one proving BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE actually resolves and signs).\n2. `beadle-daemon verify \u003cfile\u003e` added (new files — flagging since these two weren't in the amended write-set the way Makefile was). Defaults to resolving the authorizer key from daemon.json (same as beadle-daemon itself would), `--signer` overrides for an ad-hoc check. Reports good/missing/wrong-key/key-expired/invalid, exits non-zero on anything but good. Verified by hand: unsigned → \"missing\", signed with no --signer → \"good\" via daemon.json resolution.\n3. Makefile SHELL_SCRIPTS now discovers by shebang (word-boundary sh/bash/dash/zsh/ksh) instead of `*.sh` — confirmed via `comm -3` that the only diff from the old glob is scripts/beadle-sysreport, nothing lost or spuriously added. `make lint-shell` now includes it and passes.\n\nI tried to submit the round-2 result but `ethos mission show m-2026-08-31-005` still reports \"Round: 1 of 2\" and only round 1's result on file — `ethos mission result --file ... --verify` for round 2 was refused (\"result round 2 does not match mission ... current round 1\"). Looks like round 1 needs a reflection + `ethos mission advance` on your side before I can submit round 2's result. The round-2 result YAML is ready at `.tmp/missions/results/m-2026-08-31-005-round2.yaml` — let me know once you've advanced it and I'll submit immediately, or advance it yourself if that's faster.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"Round 2 done and committed; mission still shows round 1 in ethos","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"fad97a5dc7a5342b6ff178d411db94ca8e2eb84bb444799e6b0e8fccbbeb05d1","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"All three round-2 findings are fixed and committe…\",\"message\":\"All three round-2 findings are fixed and committed on feat/recipe-tooling, `make check` green (shellcheck now sweeps script..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:04:22.431576998Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arecipe-tooling-0eaee18fe59bc3d7","agent_type":"recipe-tooling","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"git status --short \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline main..HEAD"},"tool_input_hash":"962b882266b2fda254a5924f9b82c84339bccb5e72543d6feee9e2be035e7b40","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"git status --short \\u0026\\u0026 git log --oneline main..HEAD\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:04:49.463360943Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Drive beadle-daemon's recipe tooling end to end in a disposable sandbox.\n# Usage: verify-recipe-path.sh [--dry-run] [--repo DIR] [--keep]\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Safety class: READ-ONLY with respect to the operator's real state. It never\n# writes outside its own mktemp sandbox, never touches ~/.punt-labs/beadle, and\n# never touches the real GnuPG keyring. It builds nothing in the repo.\n#\n# Four operations in here are dangerous if their guards are removed. Each guard\n# is load-bearing, not defensive clutter:\n#\n#  1. rm -rf on the sandbox. Guarded by assert_sandbox, which refuses any path\n#     that is not an existing directory matching the exact mktemp template.\n#     Without it, an empty $SANDBOX would make this `rm -rf /`-adjacent.\n#  2. gpgconf --kill gpg-agent. Scoped by an explicit GNUPGHOME that\n#     assert_sandbox has already validated. If GNUPGHOME were empty or\n#     unvalidated, gpgconf falls back to the DEFAULT home and would kill the\n#     operator's real gpg-agent out from under other sessions.\n#  3. chmod -R. Same guard. The Go module cache inside a scratch HOME is\n#     read-only, so removal needs write bits restored first -- but a recursive\n#     chmod against an unvalidated path is exactly how a home directory gets\n#     opened up.\n#  4. HOME reassignment. Asserted to sit inside the sandbox before any\n#     subcommand runs, so `init` cannot write a real daemon.json.\n#\n# The test passphrase is read from `pass beadle/passphrase-test-phrase` rather\n# than hardcoded, so no secret lives in this file and the run exercises the\n# same credential backend beadle uses on Linux.\n\nreadonly SANDBOX_TEMPLATE='/tmp/bg-recipe-XXXXXX'\nreadonly SANDBOX_GLOB='/tmp/bg-recipe-'          # prefix assert_sandbox requires\nreadonly PASS_ENTRY='beadle/passphrase-test-phrase'\n\nDRY_RUN=false\nKEEP=false\nREPO_DIR=\"${HOME}/Coding/punt-labs/beadle\"\n\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --dry-run) DRY_RUN=true; shift ;;\n    --keep)    KEEP=true; shift ;;\n    --repo)    REPO_DIR=\"${2:?--repo needs a directory}\"; shift 2 ;;\n    -h|--help) sed -n '2,3p' \"$0\"; exit 0 ;;\n    *)         printf 'unknown argument: %s\\n' \"$1\" \u003e\u00262; exit 2 ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\nPASS_COUNT=0\nFAIL_COUNT=0\nSKIP_COUNT=0\nSANDBOX=''\n\nok()      { printf '  \\033[32mPASS\\033[0m  %s\\n' \"$1\"; PASS_COUNT=$((PASS_COUNT + 1)); }\nbad()     { printf '  \\033[31mFAIL\\033[0m  %s\\n' \"$1\"; FAIL_COUNT=$((FAIL_COUNT + 1)); }\nskipped() { printf '  \\033[33mSKIP\\033[0m  %s\\n' \"$1\"; SKIP_COUNT=$((SKIP_COUNT + 1)); }\nsection() { printf '\\n\\033[1m%s\\033[0m\\n' \"$1\"; }\ndie()     { printf 'error: %s\\n' \"$1\" \u003e\u00262; exit 2; }\n\n# Refuse to operate on anything that is not our own sandbox. Every destructive\n# operation below calls this first. It must stay strict: a loosened check here\n# silently re-arms rm -rf, recursive chmod, and the gpg-agent kill.\nassert_sandbox() {\n  local path=\"${1:-}\"\n  [[ -n \"${path}\" ]]                     || die 'sandbox path is empty'\n  [[ \"${path}\" == \"${SANDBOX_GLOB}\"* ]]  || die \"refusing to touch ${path}: outside ${SANDBOX_GLOB}*\"\n  [[ \"${path}\" != *..* ]]                || die \"refusing to touch ${path}: contains ..\"\n  [[ -d \"${path}\" ]]                     || die \"refusing to touch ${path}: not a directory\"\n}\n\ncleanup() {\n  [[ -n \"${SANDBOX}\" ]] || return 0\n  if \"${KEEP}\"; then\n    printf '\\n  sandbox kept at %s\\n' \"${SANDBOX}\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  assert_sandbox \"${SANDBOX}\"\n  if [[ -d \"${SANDBOX}/gpg\" ]]; then\n    GNUPGHOME=\"${SANDBOX}/gpg\" gpgconf --kill gpg-agent \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || true\n  fi\n  chmod -R u+w \"${SANDBOX}\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true\n  rm -rf -- \"${SANDBOX}\"\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\n\n# run_check \u003clabel\u003e \u003cexpected-exit\u003e \u003ccmd...\u003e\n# Captures the status of the command under test directly. Never pipe a command\n# under test: `cmd | tail` yields tail's status, which reported a FAILING\n# command as exit 0 when this sequence was first run by hand.\nCHECK_OUT=''\nrun_check() {\n  local label=\"$1\" want=\"$2\"; shift 2\n  local rc=0\n  set +e\n  CHECK_OUT=$(\"$@\" 2\u003e\u00261)\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  if [[ \"${rc}\" -eq \"${want}\" ]]; then\n    ok \"${label} (exit ${rc})\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  bad \"${label}: wanted exit ${want}, got ${rc}\"\n  printf '        %s\\n' \"${CHECK_OUT:0:300}\"\n  return 0   # keep going; the summary is the verdict\n}\n\n# --- preflight -------------------------------------------------------------\n\nsection 'Preflight'\n\n[[ -d \"${REPO_DIR}\" ]] || die \"repo not found: ${REPO_DIR} (pass --repo)\"\nDAEMON=\"${REPO_DIR}/beadle-daemon\"\nRECIPE_SRC=\"${REPO_DIR}/examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml\"\n\n[[ -x \"${DAEMON}\" ]]     || die \"beadle-daemon not built. Run: make -C ${REPO_DIR} build-daemon\"\n[[ -f \"${RECIPE_SRC}\" ]] || die \"missing example recipe: ${RECIPE_SRC}\"\ncommand -v gpg  \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || die 'gpg not on PATH'\ncommand -v pass \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || die 'pass not on PATH'\n\nok \"beadle-daemon present\"\nok \"example recipe present\"\nok \"gpg present ($(gpg --version | head -1))\"\n\nif ! TEST_PASSPHRASE=[REDACTED:env-secret]
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:04:56.722848409Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; rm -f \u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/verify-recipe-path.sh; chmod +x .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh; echo \"=== shellcheck ===\"; shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh 2\u003e\u00261 | head -20; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"=== dry run ===\"; .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh --dry-run 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -14","description":"Shellcheck and dry-run the new script"},"tool_input_hash":"1519f0ae0cf6203ad8ee19bed7fa48888ee2f23bfea250f207d88bf16af1e126","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; rm -f \\u003crepo\\u003e/.tmp/verify-recipe-path.sh; chmod +x .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh; echo \\\"=== shellcheck ===\\\"; shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR .bin/verify-recipe-pa..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:05:04.489172095Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-047","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -32; echo \"SCRIPT EXIT: ${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"","description":"Run the verification script for real"},"tool_input_hash":"229645f81e21a1efcabac0ffa8192ca7bffd84e1934420acbacc608775e32632","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs; .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh 2\\u003e\\u00261 | tail -32; echo \\\"SCRIPT EXIT: ${PIPESTATUS[0]}\\\"\",\"description\":\"Run the verification script for real\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:05:37.914993049Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-055","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Review the .bin verification script","name":"review-script","prompt":"Review `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` in ~/Coding/punt-labs (the workspace meta-repo, not beadle). I wrote it; the operator asked for it to be properly reviewed. Be adversarial — I am not looking for validation.\n\n**What it does.** Drives `beadle-daemon`'s new recipe tooling (`init`, `sign`, and a `verify` subcommand that does not exist yet) end to end inside a disposable sandbox, so the operator-facing path is checked repeatably instead of by hand.\n\n**Current state:** `shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR` exits 0. `--dry-run` works. A real run reports 19 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped.\n\n**Why the operator asked for review specifically.** Their words about my first draft: \"those operations are not particularly safe.\" They were right. It performs four genuinely dangerous operations, and I rewrote it so each is gated by one `assert_sandbox` function:\n\n1. `rm -rf` on the sandbox in an EXIT trap\n2. `gpgconf --kill gpg-agent` — with an unvalidated `GNUPGHOME`, gpgconf falls back to the DEFAULT home and would kill the operator's real agent out from under other live sessions\n3. `chmod -R u+w` — needed because a Go module cache inside a scratch HOME is read-only, but a recursive chmod on an unvalidated path is how a home directory gets opened up\n4. reassigning `HOME`, so a subcommand cannot write a real `~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json`\n\n**Attack the guards.** `assert_sandbox` requires a non-empty path, a `/tmp/bg-recipe-` prefix, no `..`, and an existing directory. I want you to try to break it: symlinks (is `/tmp/bg-recipe-x` a symlink to `$HOME` a problem?), TOCTOU between the check and the `rm`, `mktemp` failing, the trap firing before `SANDBOX` is assigned, the trap firing mid-`mkdir`, a `SANDBOX` containing whitespace or a newline, `TMPDIR` being redirected (this repo sets `TMPDIR` via `.envrc` — does that change where `mktemp -d /tmp/...` lands, and does the guard still hold?). If any of these defeats a guard, that is the finding I most want.\n\n**Also review against `.bin/CLAUDE.md` conventions.** `set -euo pipefail` is required and present. It is single-repo, so I deliberately did NOT source `lib/safety.sh` — that library checks busy/dirty/open-PR across repos, which does not apply. Tell me if you disagree. Convention also requires a `README.md` catalog entry with purpose, flags, and safety class, which I have NOT added — please add it, in the style of the existing entries, and put it in whichever functional group fits (it is closest to the read-only/test group).\n\n**Specific things to judge:**\n- The secret handling. The test passphrase comes from `pass beadle/passphrase-test-phrase`, never hardcoded. It gets written to `$HOME/.punt-labs/beadle/secrets/gpg-passphrase` inside the sandbox to exercise beadle's real credential chain. There is an assertion that the passphrase never appears in command output. Is that assertion actually sufficient, and is writing it to disk at all the right call?\n- `run_check` toggles `set +e`/`set -e` around the command under test to capture its status. Is that correct under `pipefail`, and is there a cleaner idiom?\n- I use `perl -pi -e` for an in-place edit because BSD and GNU `sed -i` disagree on the backup-suffix argument. Is perl a reasonable dependency for `.bin`, or should this be done differently?\n- Portability: the operator runs Linux, but `.bin` scripts are shared and macOS is a supported platform. The `stat` call has a BSD fallback; look for anything else that is GNU-only.\n\n**Do not soften the script's findings.** The two SKIPs are real: there is no `verify` subcommand, so an operator cannot check a recipe's signature without starting the daemon. That skip should stay visible, not be quietly dropped.\n\nReport findings with file:line and severity. Fix what is clearly wrong, add the README entry, run `shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR` and the script itself, and commit on a branch off main in the workspace repo. Do not push. If you think the whole approach is wrong, say so plainly — that is a more useful answer than polishing something misconceived.","subagent_type":"adb"},"tool_input_hash":"2892a14d6b2d67375cbfa2fc512863c895e8d39dcb8d20a5689f71f28f6ba0d8","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Review the .bin verification script\",\"name\":\"review-script\",\"prompt\":\"Review `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` in ~/Coding/punt-labs (the workspace meta-repo, not beadle). I wrote it; the o..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:05:40.933887454Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"areview-script-b1f0d2e3686fe8d3","agent_type":"review-script","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-055","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh"},"tool_input_hash":"f320bc2a24b2759f92c5905d2e6fa7bba3a6431e7403a0c59816b5879ef033a9","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:05:43.629898051Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"areview-script-b1f0d2e3686fe8d3","agent_type":"review-script","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-055","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/.bin/CLAUDE.md"},"tool_input_hash":"26a159436594f25fef8c3bb70b1d246df9c17a344a66294f29d1e6643cf95c35","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/.bin/CLAUDE.md\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:05:43.964198792Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"areview-script-b1f0d2e3686fe8d3","agent_type":"review-script","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-055","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/.bin/README.md"},"tool_input_hash":"ddf63d7be7af9bbcd1ed448420b491e6b88b38ad0a1d1b5149d7733e245d146c","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/.bin/README.md\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:05:51.681278752Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-055","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Correction to my round-2 brief before you act on …","message":"Correction to my round-2 brief before you act on item 1 — do not fix a non-problem.\n\nI built a repeatable harness (`.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` in the workspace repo) and ran the whole path against a real passphrase-protected key, with the passphrase stored where beadle's own credential chain looks for it (`$HOME/.punt-labs/beadle/secrets/gpg-passphrase`, mode 600, inside a sandboxed HOME). Result:\n\n```\nPASS  signed with a protected key via the gpg-passphrase credential\nPASS  passphrase does not appear in command output\n19 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped\n```\n\n**So the protected-key capability is correct and complete.** My original failure was purely that I had not stored the credential — exactly what your `sign_cmd.go:84` comment describes. The `ErrNotFound` → empty-passphrase decision is right, and the secret does not leak into output.\n\n**Item 1 therefore narrows to the error message alone.** When `detachSign` fails and the resolved passphrase was empty, the message should name `gpg-passphrase` and the resolution order. Nothing else about that path needs touching. Do not add a flag, do not change the credential lookup, do not weaken the empty-passphrase behaviour.\n\nItems 2 (`verify` subcommand) and 3 (the `Makefile` glob) stand unchanged. The harness already asserts on `verify` and currently reports two SKIPs for it, so it will start exercising your implementation the moment it lands:\n\n```\nSKIP  no 'verify' subcommand: an operator cannot check a signature without\nSKIP    starting the daemon and reading its logs\n```\n\nThose SKIPs turn into three real checks — valid accepted, tampered rejected, unsigned rejected — so build `verify` to exit non-zero on anything but a good signature.\n\nTwo other things the harness confirmed, so you know they are already good and need no attention: `daemon.json` lands at mode 600, and the committed example recipe correctly ships unsigned.\n\nApologies for the churn on item 1 — I reported a symptom before isolating its cause, which is the thing I keep telling reviewers not to do.","recipient":"recipe-tooling","summary":"Correction: protected-key signing works","to":"recipe-tooling","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"517c39f0c6deaf25f625593bd4187eeccd3300668e5c4069f36a9443250ba9aa","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Correction to my round-2 brief before you act on …\",\"message\":\"Correction to my round-2 brief before you act on item 1 — do not fix a non-problem.\\n\\nI built a repeatable harness (`.bi..."}
