{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:06:19.879601343Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-08-31-055","contract_id":"m-2026-08-31-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; mkdir -p .tmp/missions/reflections; cat \u003e .tmp/missions/reflections/r1.yaml \u003c\u003c'YAML'\nmission: m-2026-08-31-005\nround: 1\nauthor: claude\nconverging: true\nsignals:\n  - \"Round 1 accepted. Verified independently: make check clean, and the real binary driven end to end in an isolated HOME/GNUPGHOME. init wrote the fingerprint, a second init exited 1 naming --force, --force worked, sign reported round-trip verified and produced a real signature.\"\n  - \"The round-trip proof is genuinely wired, not merely claimed -- sign calls VerifySignature on its own output before writing. This was the single most important constraint in the brief and it was honored.\"\n  - \"CanonicalCommandBytes was reused rather than reimplemented, as required. Signing and verification cannot disagree on canonical bytes.\"\n  - \"Worker escalated two items rather than reaching outside its write-set: the Makefile *.sh glob missing scripts/beadle-sysreport, and confirmation that beadle-5ma blocks usefulness off this machine. Both correct calls; write-set amended to include Makefile.\"\n  - \"Worker's design change -- sign --signer taking only a 40-hex fingerprint -- was forced by a gosec exclusion boundary, but the reasoning it gave is better than the constraint: the same string signs and re-verifies, removing a class of mismatch. Accepted and kept.\"\n  - \"LEADER ERROR: I reported a protected-key signing failure as a round-2 finding before isolating its cause. The capability was correct; I had simply not stored the gpg-passphrase credential. Corrected to the worker before it acted, narrowing item 1 to the error message alone. I should have isolated before reporting -- the exact discipline I have been holding reviewers to all session.\"\nrecommendation: advance\nYAML\nethos mission reflect m-2026-08-31-005 --file .tmp/missions/reflections/r1.yaml 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2; ethos mission advance m-2026-08-31-005 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2","description":"Reflect on round 1 and advance the mission"},"tool_input_hash":"672fe6efc2ec0e56d08437baa79e043858858485c06995c97c59ece7d50f7a1f","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; mkdir -p .tmp/missions/reflections; cat \\u003e .tmp/missions/reflections/r1.yaml \\u003c\\u003c'YAML'\\nmission: m-2026-08-31-005\\nround: 1\\nauthor: claude\\ncon..."}
