{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:10:07.269759751Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arecipe-tooling-0eaee18fe59bc3d7","agent_type":"recipe-tooling","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"mission: m-2026-08-31-006\nround: 1\nauthor: bwk\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.95\nfiles_changed:\n  - path: Makefile\n    added: 15\n    removed: 7\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/init_cmd.go\n    added: 97\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/init_cmd_test.go\n    added: 136\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd.go\n    added: 144\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd_test.go\n    added: 189\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd.go\n    added: 121\n    removed: 0\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd_test.go\n    added: 128\n    removed: 0\n  - path: examples/recipes/README.md\n    added: 100\n    removed: 0\n  - path: examples/recipes/docs-ask.yaml\n    added: 33\n    removed: 0\n  - path: examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml\n    added: 32\n    removed: 0\n  - path: internal/daemon/spawner_test.go\n    added: 76\n    removed: 0\n  - path: internal/daemon/templates.go\n    added: 28\n    removed: 4\n  - path: internal/daemon/templates_test.go\n    added: 55\n    removed: 1\n  - path: scripts/beadle-sysreport\n    added: 26\n    removed: 0\nevidence:\n  - name: make check (shellcheck incl. scripts/beadle-sysreport via shebang discovery, go vet, staticcheck, golangci-lint 0 issues, govulncheck 0 vulnerabilities, markdownlint 0 errors, go test -race -count=1 ./... all green)\n    status: pass\n  - name: .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh run independently against this branch's build (make build-daemon at repo root) — 22 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped, including verify accept/reject/unsigned and the passphrase-protected-key path\n    status: pass\n  - name: go test -race -count=1 ./cmd/beadle-daemon/... ./internal/daemon/... — full table incl. real-GPG round-trip, tamper detection, passphrase-protected key (failure message + BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE happy path), http-vs-stdio byte-identical MCP config emission, envOverrides-never-logged\n    status: pass\n  - name: manual end-to-end walkthrough — init --fingerprint, verify (missing) on unsigned recipe, sign, verify again with no --signer resolving from daemon.json (good), second init refused without --force then succeeding with --force\n    status: pass\nopen_questions: []\nprose: |\n  Successor to m-2026-08-31-005, closed escalated for a write_set gap\n  (Makefile, verify_cmd.go, verify_cmd_test.go authorized in conversation\n  but never added to the immutable contract). No code changes were made\n  between the two missions -- this result covers the same, already-\n  reviewed work, now declared against a write_set that actually matches\n  git diff --name-only main..HEAD.\n\n  Delivered:\n  - beadle-daemon init: writes daemon.json from an ethos handle or literal\n    fingerprint via daemon.Config.ResolveOwnerKeyID, refuses to clobber\n    without --force, writes nothing when the owner config doesn't resolve.\n  - beadle-daemon sign: canonicalizes via daemon.CanonicalCommandBytes (the\n    same function VerifySignature uses, never reimplemented), signs via\n    the system keyring, calls VerifySignature on the result before writing\n    anything to disk. A passphrase-protected signing key with no stored\n    credential fails with a message naming the gpg-passphrase credential\n    and all three resolution paths (keychain, secrets file,\n    BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE) -- never the passphrase itself. Verified with a\n    real protected key both ways: the failure message, and successful\n    signing once BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE resolves it.\n  - beadle-daemon verify: resolves the authorizer key from daemon.json by\n    default (the same key beadle-daemon itself trusts), or an explicit\n    --signer. Reports good/missing/wrong-key/key-expired/invalid, exits\n    non-zero on anything but good.\n  - MCPServerConfig extended with Type/URL/Headers (all omitempty);\n    exact-JSON tests prove stdio entries emit byte-identical output and\n    an http entry (context7) emits only type/url/headers.\n  - context7 registered as an http MCP server; CONTEXT7_API_KEY reaches\n    the worker via the existing env_vars allowlist + resolveEnvVars +\n    Spawner.Run envOverrides mechanism, never written to a log line --\n    proven with a new regression test against a fake claude binary.\n  - examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml (cli runner) + docs-ask.yaml (claude\n    runner, context7, required question arg) + scripts/beadle-sysreport\n    (shellcheck-clean, disk free + CPU load as JSON) + README.md\n    documenting init/sign/verify end to end. Both recipes ship unsigned\n    on purpose.\n  - Makefile: SHELL_SCRIPTS now discovers scripts by shebang instead of\n    *.sh, so the extensionless scripts/beadle-sysreport (it must be named\n    exactly that once deployed, matching the recipe's binary: field) is\n    swept into lint-shell/make check. Verified via comm -3 that the only\n    change from the old glob is that one file.\n\n  Both independent harness runs (mine and the leader's) against the same\n  branch build report 22 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. make check is green\n  end to end. No open design questions remain.\n","file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/missions/results/m-2026-08-31-006-round1.yaml"},"tool_input_hash":"7dfa52c9863e014e604c1f9f71dd9962966ecd11a2c04cf62218f44cbc01ec7b","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"mission: m-2026-08-31-006\\nround: 1\\nauthor: bwk\\nverdict: pass\\nconfidence: 0.95\\nfiles_changed:\\n  - path: Makefile\\n    added: 15\\n    removed: 7\\n  - path: cmd/beadle-daemon/init_cmd.g..."}
