{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:10:40.989186738Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; ethos mission close m-2026-08-31-006 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2; bd update beadle-7gm --status=open 2\u003e\u00261 \u003e/dev/null; echo \"--- branch ready ---\"; git log --oneline main..HEAD | wc -l; git diff --stat main..HEAD | tail -1","description":"Close the mission and confirm branch state"},"tool_input_hash":"9d2441c9d6951ea92b3b5f99b30500e2893a63bb7808dc0ebe2519f53521b155","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; ethos mission close m-2026-08-31-006 2\\u003e\\u00261 | tail -2; bd update beadle-7gm --status=open 2\\u003e\\u00261 \\u003e/dev/null; echo \\\"--- branch ready ---..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:11:02.8741768Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Code review the recipe tooling diff","name":"rev-code","prompt":"Review the diff of `feat/recipe-tooling` against `main` in \u003crepo\u003e. Get it with `git diff main..HEAD` — 14 files, +1180/-12, 9 commits.\n\n**What it adds.** Operator-facing tooling for `beadle-daemon` recipes (GPG-signed YAML command files), which previously could not be authored at all:\n- `beadle-daemon init` — writes `~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json` naming the key that authorizes recipes\n- `beadle-daemon sign` — canonicalizes a recipe, signs it, verifies its own output before writing\n- `beadle-daemon verify` — checks a recipe's signature without starting the daemon\n- `MCPServerConfig` extended for http transport; `context7` registered\n- two example recipes, `scripts/beadle-sysreport`, and a `Makefile` change discovering shell scripts by shebang instead of `*.sh`\n\n**Security-relevant context you need.** This is the tooling around a trust boundary, so ordinary code-quality review is not the whole job:\n\n- The signed payload is `yaml.Marshal` of the `Command` struct with `Signature` cleared, produced by `daemon.CanonicalCommandBytes`. `sign` MUST call that function rather than reproducing the marshaling. If signing and verification ever compute canonical bytes differently, every recipe silently fails to load and the failure presents as a bad key. Confirm it actually calls it.\n- `MCPServerConfig` gained `Type`/`URL`/`Headers` with `omitempty`. The existing stdio entries (`ethos`, `beadle-email`, `biff`) must emit **byte-identical** JSON to before, because Claude Code parses that config and a shape change breaks worker spawning in a way that will not look like an MCP problem.\n- A `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` now reaches spawned workers. Check every path that could stringify env — logs, error strings, `Pipeline.Error`. A leak here is the finding I most want.\n- `sign` resolves a `gpg-passphrase` credential. Confirm the passphrase cannot reach a log line, an error message, or a process argument list.\n\n**Already verified, so do not spend time re-confirming:** `make check` passes; `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` reports 22 passed / 0 failed against a real build, covering init happy-path, clobber refusal, `--force`, sign round-trip, verify accept/tamper/unsigned, and protected-key signing via the credential chain. What I have NOT done is read this code closely for quality, which is your job.\n\nJudge it against `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`'s invariants, `CLAUDE.md`, and `../punt-kit/standards/go.md` — particularly the Go standard's rules on error wrapping with context, compile-time interface assertions, no `panic` in library code, and small interfaces.\n\nReport findings with file:line and a concrete fix. Be specific about severity: I want to know which findings block a PR and which are polish. If you find nothing material, say so plainly rather than manufacturing findings — but this is a signing tool, so look hard at the crypto-adjacent paths before concluding that.","subagent_type":"code-reviewer"},"tool_input_hash":"a12f82f85c3dd654ca90ea0223357b0fc2f342069a146f8b6ba81ccdcb736377","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Code review the recipe tooling diff\",\"name\":\"rev-code\",\"prompt\":\"Review the diff of `feat/recipe-tooling` against `main` in \\u003crepo\\u003e. Get it with `git diff main..HEAD` — 14 f..."}
