{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:12:03.738759916Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"areview-script-b1f0d2e3686fe8d3","agent_type":"review-script","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe/.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh","new_string":"#  4. HOME reassignment. Asserted to sit inside the sandbox before any\n#     subcommand runs, so `init` cannot write a real daemon.json.\n#\n# assert_sandbox also rejects a symlink at the sandbox path outright (-d\n# alone follows symlinks), so a swapped-in symlink can't turn the chmod/rm\n# above into a recursive operation on their target. SANDBOX is only ever\n# mktemp's own output, never user-supplied, so today this closes a path that\n# does not exist yet -- it's there so it still holds if that changes. The\n# remaining TOCTOU window between the check and the destructive calls relies\n# on /tmp's sticky bit: only this script's own uid can rename/replace a path\n# it owns underneath /tmp, so another local user cannot race the swap in.\n#\n# The test passphrase is read from `pass beadle/passphrase-test-phrase` rather\n# than hardcoded, so no secret lives in this file and the run exercises the\n# same credential backend beadle uses on Linux.","old_string":"#  4. HOME reassignment. Asserted to sit inside the sandbox before any\n#     subcommand runs, so `init` cannot write a real daemon.json.\n#\n# The test passphrase is read from `pass beadle/passphrase-test-phrase` rather\n# than hardcoded, so no secret lives in this file and the run exercises the\n# same credential backend beadle uses on Linux.","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"14d21419893b8469e86cdaa02cf1d392264c5761bedaff25a9db50bd87f0b400","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe/.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh\",\"new_string\":\"#  4. HOME reassignment. Asserted to sit inside the sandbox before any\\n#     subcommand ..."}
