{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:08.074243885Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-silent-0b5e7e5e3c6716f9","agent_type":"rev-silent","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"go build -o .tmp/bd ./cmd/beadle-daemon/ \u0026\u0026 .tmp/bd verify examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml --signer 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567 2\u003e\u00261 | head -30; echo \"EXIT=$?\"","description":"Run verify to observe real operator output"},"tool_input_hash":"b426e116adf09dde88d67c5dfa7842cf2b5a090a2b666e30202b5cd41fb5cfca","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"go build -o .tmp/bd ./cmd/beadle-daemon/ \\u0026\\u0026 .tmp/bd verify examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml --signer 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567 2\\u003e\\u00261 | head -30; echo \\\"EXI..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:14.588890149Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"areview-script-b1f0d2e3686fe8d3","agent_type":"review-script","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nchore(.bin): add verify-recipe-path.sh, hardened after adversarial review\n\nAdds the beadle-daemon recipe-tooling smoke script (init/sign/verify\nend to end in a disposable mktemp sandbox) with fixes found during\nreview:\n\n- assert_sandbox now rejects a symlink at the sandbox path outright\n  (-d alone follows symlinks) -- defense in depth for the three\n  destructive operations it gates (rm -rf, chmod -R, gpgconf --kill),\n  even though SANDBOX is only ever mktemp's own output today.\n- Fixed an ordering bug in the passphrase-protected-signing check: the\n  two failure branches printed a raw command-output snippet BEFORE\n  checking whether that output contained the test passphrase, so a\n  real leak would have already been echoed to the terminal by the\n  time the leak assertion ran. The leak check now runs first, and a\n  detected leak withholds the diagnostic instead of printing it.\n- Replaced perl -pi -e (an undocumented new .bin dependency) with the\n  sed_inplace() GNU/BSD helper already used by audit-install-shas.sh\n  and audit-catalog-pins.sh for the identical portability problem.\n- Replaced the ad hoc `sed -n '2,3p' \"$0\"` --help handler with a real\n  usage() function -- fixes a confirmed missing-help-handler finding\n  from .bin/health/script-safety.py (verified before and after).\n- chmod 700 on the sandboxed $HOME, not just $GNUPGHOME, so the\n  passphrase file's protection doesn't rest solely on the parent\n  sandbox directory's mode.\n- run_check now uses `if var=$(cmd); then ... else ...; fi` instead of\n  toggling set +e/-e, avoiding any window where errexit is disabled.\n- Catalogs the script in README.md as \"destructive (sandbox-scoped)\",\n  not read-only -- it does mutate the filesystem (mktemp sandbox,\n  minted GPG keys, a written passphrase file), just never outside its\n  own disposable sandbox.\n\nVerified: shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR clean; script-safety.py reports\nzero violations (confirmed missing-help-handler both before the fix\nand cleared after); a real (non-dry-run) run against a freshly built\nbeadle-daemon passes 22/22 with 0 skipped (the daemon now ships a\n`verify` subcommand, so the two SKIPs from the original report no\nlonger trigger); sandbox and daemon.json confirmed cleaned up after\nthe run, nothing leaked into the real beadle checkout.\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the reviewed and fixed script"},"tool_input_hash":"d57dd3247d184d379163b959959a17d88df6743540faf86e5108357f40bdd920","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nchore(.bin): add verify-recipe-path.sh, hardened after adversarial review\\n\\..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:14.642312761Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-silent-0b5e7e5e3c6716f9","agent_type":"rev-silent","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":".tmp/bd verify examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml --signer 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567 \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; echo \"verify(missing sig) EXIT=$?\"; .tmp/bd verify examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml --signer notafingerprint \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; echo \"verify(bad signer) EXIT=$?\"; .tmp/bd verify /nonexistent.yaml --signer 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567 \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; echo \"verify(no file) EXIT=$?\"; rm -f .tmp/bd","description":"Check verify exit codes"},"tool_input_hash":"a7136c1e9e64131b3fbdc2b1451dfe757afe729192ad966264bf1c39a2faafc7","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\".tmp/bd verify examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml --signer 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567 \\u003e/dev/null 2\\u003e\\u00261; echo \\\"verify(missing sig) EXIT=$?\\\"; .tmp/bd verify exampl..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:24.6212373Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-invariant-d1f64b9173a77bf7","agent_type":"rev-invariant","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"mkdir -p \u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/canoncheck \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e \u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/canoncheck/main.go \u003c\u003c'EOF'\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"gopkg.in/yaml.v3\"\n\n\t\"github.com/punt-labs/beadle/internal/daemon\"\n)\n\n// fixpoint mimics runSign: decode source -\u003e canon1 (signed bytes) -\u003e\n// set Signature -\u003e marshal -\u003e write file. Then mimics loadCommand:\n// decode written file -\u003e canon2. If canon1 != canon2 the daemon would\n// reject a file `sign` just declared round-trip verified.\nfunc fixpoint(label string, src []byte) {\n\tvar c1 daemon.Command\n\tdec := yaml.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(src))\n\tdec.KnownFields(true)\n\tif err := dec.Decode(\u0026c1); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s DECODE-ERR %v\\n\", label, err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tcanon1, err := daemon.CanonicalCommandBytes(\u0026c1)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s CANON-ERR %v\\n\", label, err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tc1.Signature = \"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\nFAKE\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\"\n\twritten, err := yaml.Marshal(\u0026c1)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s MARSHAL-ERR %v\\n\", label, err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tvar c2 daemon.Command\n\tdec2 := yaml.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(written))\n\tdec2.KnownFields(true)\n\tif err := dec2.Decode(\u0026c2); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s RELOAD-DECODE-ERR %v\\n\", label, err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tcanon2, err := daemon.CanonicalCommandBytes(\u0026c2)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s RELOAD-CANON-ERR %v\\n\", label, err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif bytes.Equal(canon1, canon2) {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s OK\\n\", label)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tfmt.Printf(\"%-24s ***MISMATCH***\\n--- signed bytes ---\\n%s\\n--- reloaded bytes ---\\n%s\\n\", label, canon1, canon2)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tfor _, p := range os.Args[1:] {\n\t\tb, err := os.ReadFile(p)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Println(\"read:\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfixpoint(p, b)\n\t}\n\n\tcases := map[string]string{\n\t\t\"long-folded-prompt\": \"name: x\\nrunner: claude\\noutput_schema: text\\nbudget:\\n  rounds: 1\\nprompt: \u003e-\\n  \" + longLine() + \"\\n\",\n\t\t\"trailing-space\":     \"name: x\\nrunner: claude\\noutput_schema: text\\nprompt: \\\"line one   \\\\nline two\\\"\\n\",\n\t\t\"tabs-in-prompt\":     \"name: x\\nrunner: claude\\noutput_schema: text\\nprompt: \\\"a\\\\tb\\\\nc\\\\td\\\"\\n\",\n\t\t\"crlf-in-prompt\":     \"name: x\\nrunner: claude\\noutput_schema: text\\nprompt: \\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\"\\n\",\n\t\t\"unicode-prompt\":     \"name: x\\nrunner: claude\\noutput_schema: text\\nprompt: \\\"héllo — wörld \\\\u00a0nbsp\\\"\\n\",\n\t\t\"schema-float-int\":   \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema:\\n  maximum: 1.0\\n  minimum: 0\\n  scale: 1e100\\n\",\n\t\t\"schema-nonstr-keys\": \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema:\\n  1: one\\n  true: yes\\n\",\n\t\t\"schema-nested-map\":  \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema:\\n  z: 1\\n  a:\\n    q: 2\\n    b: [1,2,3]\\n\",\n\t\t\"anchor-alias\":       \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema: \u0026s\\n  a: 1\\nfixed_args: [\\\"--x\\\"]\\n\",\n\t\t\"time-like-string\":   \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema:\\n  when: 2026-08-31\\n  ver: 1.10\\n  on: yes\\n\",\n\t\t\"multiline-literal\":  \"name: x\\nrunner: claude\\noutput_schema: text\\nprompt: |\\n  line1\\n  line2\\n\",\n\t\t\"empty-string-desc\":  \"name: x\\ndescription: \\\"\\\"\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema: text\\n\",\n\t\t\"null-fields\":        \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema: text\\nfixed_args: null\\ntools: []\\n\",\n\t\t\"very-long-plain\":    \"name: \" + longLine() + \"\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema: text\\n\",\n\t\t\"binary-b64\":         \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema:\\n  blob: !!binary |\\n    R0lG\\n\",\n\t\t\"deep-indent\":        \"name: x\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema:\\n  a:\\n    b:\\n      c:\\n        d:\\n          e: \" + longLine() + \"\\n\",\n\t}\n\tfor k, v := range cases {\n\t\tfixpoint(k, []byte(v))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc longLine() string {\n\ts := \"\"\n\tfor i := 0; i \u003c 30; i++ {\n\t\ts += \"wordwordword \"\n\t}\n\treturn s + \"end\"\n}\nEOF\ngo run ./.tmp/canoncheck examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml examples/recipes/docs-ask.yaml 2\u003e\u00261 | head -80"},"tool_input_hash":"e11792445c390a0e1bfec76c723336e5104c79b7583b42991b3e1f314a95012d","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"mkdir -p \\u003crepo\\u003e/.tmp/canoncheck \\u0026\\u0026 cat \\u003e \\u003crepo\\u003e/.tmp/canoncheck/main.go \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\npackage main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"bytes\\\"\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\n..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:32.755685891Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-silent-0b5e7e5e3c6716f9","agent_type":"rev-silent","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"grep -n \"keychainGet(name)\" internal/secret/secret.go; grep -n \"envOverrides, missingEnv\\|e.Logger.Error(\\\"declared env var\" internal/daemon/pipeline.go internal/daemon/runner.go","description":"Get exact line numbers"},"tool_input_hash":"b18af61da9b64b0ec637220e906be1346ed212c963d8b1e595cfbe3855637ab3","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"keychainGet(name)\\\" internal/secret/secret.go; grep -n \\\"envOverrides, missingEnv\\\\|e.Logger.Error(\\\\\\\"declared env var\\\" internal/daemon/pipeline.go internal/daemon/runner.go\",\"..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:54.889698021Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-invariant-d1f64b9173a77bf7","agent_type":"rev-invariant","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"sed -n 1,80p cmd/beadle-daemon/main.go \u0026\u0026 echo '=== SilenceErrors/os.Exit ===' \u0026\u0026 grep -rn \"os.Exit\\|SilenceUsage\\|SilenceErrors\\|Execute()\" cmd/beadle-daemon/*.go"},"tool_input_hash":"dc5360e9c6b7851df042a7bb334704b3a10155016c3550d02e772d57a138b644","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"sed -n 1,80p cmd/beadle-daemon/main.go \\u0026\\u0026 echo '=== SilenceErrors/os.Exit ===' \\u0026\\u0026 grep -rn \\\"os.Exit\\\\|SilenceUsage\\\\|SilenceErrors\\\\|Execute()\\\" cmd/beadle-daemon/*.go..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:14:55.77935175Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"areview-script-b1f0d2e3686fe8d3","agent_type":"review-script","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Reviewed adversarially, fixed what was wrong, add…","message":"Reviewed adversarially, fixed what was wrong, added the README entry, committed. Branch `chore/add-verify-recipe-path-script`, isolated in a worktree at `~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe` (your main checkout was on `chore/enable-biff-quarry-gitignore-fix` with a pile of unrelated uncommitted edits from the other active agents — didn't want to touch that tree or its branch, so I built off `main` in a worktree instead; `git worktree remove` it after you merge). Commit `25ccde7`, not pushed.\n\n**Findings, file:line against the original `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh`:**\n\n1. **MEDIUM — passphrase-leak check ran after the leak-prone print, not before (:271-293).** In the protected-key section, both `bad` branches printed `${LOCKED_OUT:0:200}` raw, and only *after* that did the script check whether `LOCKED_OUT` contained `TEST_PASSPHRASE`. If beadle-daemon's `sign` ever actually leaked the passphrase into an error message, this script's own diagnostic output would have already put it on the terminal/log before the assertion meant to catch that ran. Fixed: compute the leak flag first, gate the diagnostic print on it (`diag()` withholds the snippet entirely on a detected leak — I didn't try to regex-redact just the passphrase substring out of the snippet, since bash's `${var//pattern/repl}` treats `pattern` as a glob, and a real passphrase can contain glob metacharacters that would make a partial redaction unreliable).\n\n2. **LOW-MEDIUM — `perl -pi -e` for the tampered-recipe edit (:242-243).** Not in `.bin/CLAUDE.md`'s documented External Tool Requirements, and the repo already has a `sed_inplace()` helper for this exact GNU/BSD `sed -i` divergence in `audit-install-shas.sh` and `audit-catalog-pins.sh`. Replaced with the same helper — zero new dependency, matches existing convention.\n\n3. **LOW — `--help` used `sed -n '2,3p' \"$0\"` instead of a `usage()` function (:44).** Functionally fine, but `.bin/health/script-safety.py`'s `missing-help-handler` check specifically requires a `usage()` function (regex `^\\s*usage\\s*\\(\\)\\s*\\{`) plus a `-h|--help` arm — I ran the checker before and after: it *did* flag `missing-help-handler` on the original script, confirmed empirically, not just by reading the regex. Fixed with a real `usage()` function; checker now reports zero violations for this script.\n\n4. **LOW (defense-in-depth) — `assert_sandbox`'s `-d` test follows symlinks (:63-69).** I could not build a working exploit against the current script — `SANDBOX` is only ever `mktemp`'s own output, never user-supplied, and `/tmp` on this box has the sticky bit set (verified: `drwxrwxrwt`), which blocks another local uid from renaming/swapping our 0700 sandbox dir. So the realistic TOCTOU/symlink attack you asked me to try does **not** currently work. But the function is explicitly the shared gate for three destructive ops and is documented as load-bearing, so I added `[[ ! -L \"${path}\" ]]` ahead of the `-d` check anyway — cheap, correct, and it means the guard still holds if a future edit ever lets `SANDBOX` (or a copy of this function) take a path from a flag.\n\n5. **Verified, not a bug — TMPDIR doesn't affect this.** Tested directly: `TMPDIR=\u003cother dir\u003e mktemp -d \"/tmp/bg-recipe-XXXXXX\"` still lands under `/tmp/bg-recipe-*` on this box's GNU coreutils 9.4. An explicit template containing `/` overrides TMPDIR on both GNU and BSD mktemp, so the header's claim about this is correct.\n\n6. **Minor hardening — sandboxed `$HOME` wasn't explicitly `chmod 700`, only `$GNUPGHOME` was (:154).** The real protection came from the parent `SANDBOX` dir already being 0700 from `mktemp -d`, so this wasn't exploitable, but the passphrase file lives under `$HOME`, not `$GNUPGHOME` — added `chmod 700 \"${HOME}\"` alongside it as belt-and-suspenders.\n\n7. **Style, not a bug — `run_check`'s `set +e`/`set -e` toggle (:91-105).** Correct under `pipefail` (no pipe involved; the assignment's exit status is what triggers errexit, and `set +e` correctly suspends that). Replaced with `if CHECK_OUT=$(\"$@\" 2\u003e\u00261); then rc=0; else rc=$?; fi` per your ask for a cleaner idiom — avoids any window where errexit is globally disabled, in case a future edit adds an early `return` between the toggles.\n\n**On `--apply`/default-to-preview (judgment call, not a bug — flagging rather than deciding unilaterally):** `punt-kit/standards/shell.md` §Operational Safety says any script with a filesystem write outside `.tmp/` must default to preview and require `--apply`/`--yes`/a positional target. This script's default (no flags) does real work — mints real GPG keys, runs the real `init`/`sign`/`verify` — with `--dry-run` as the opt-in preview, which is literally \"the pattern this replaces\" per that standard's own wording. I did **not** add `--apply`, because every mutation here is 100% confined to the disposable sandbox (nothing persists past `--keep`, nothing touches `~/.punt-labs/beadle` or the real keyring) — a materially different risk profile than the git/GitHub/keychain/LaunchAgent categories the rule targets, and the repo already has precedent for this (`git-pull-all.sh` mutates for real on bare invocation, guarded only by `safety_check`, not `--apply`). Worth noting: `script-safety.py`'s automated check does *not* flag this script for `destructive-without-apply-or-target` — but only because of an accidental match: `${2:?--repo needs a directory}` inside the `--repo` flag's parsing incidentally matches the checker's \"required positional argument\" regex, even though `--repo` is optional. I'm flagging this as a checker false-negative, not fixing `script-safety.py` itself — that's a separate, shared script and out of scope for this review. Your call on whether this script needs `--apply` regardless of what the checker catches.\n\n**Stale claim in your brief:** the \"2 skipped\" you reported no longer reproduces. I built `beadle-daemon` fresh from this checkout (`cmd/beadle-daemon/verify_cmd.go` already exists) and ran the real script end to end: **22 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** — the `verify` subcommand exists now, so both `verify`-gated SKIPs fire the real positive/negative cases instead. Looks like `recipe-tooling` (or whoever) shipped `verify` concurrently with your draft. Confirmed sandbox and `daemon.json` were cleaned up after the run and nothing leaked into the real beadle checkout.\n\n**README:** added under §1 (closest to read-only/test group per your ask), but labeled `destructive (sandbox-scoped)` rather than bare `read-only` — it does mutate the filesystem, real GPG keys included, just never outside its own `/tmp/bg-recipe-*` dir. Calling it read-only would be inaccurate to an operator reading the table.\n\n`shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR` clean before and after. Didn't touch anything else in the shared working tree.","recipient":"main","summary":"verify-recipe-path.sh reviewed, fixed, committed (not pushed)","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"55c841edda4a4f1dcfa59ac0de69fe909070f6741f7d2ed05b911de1b2a0f768","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Reviewed adversarially, fixed what was wrong, add…\",\"message\":\"Reviewed adversarially, fixed what was wrong, added the README entry, committed. Branch `chore/add-verify-recipe-path-scrip..."}
