{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:16:58.402892584Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-invariant-d1f64b9173a77bf7","agent_type":"rev-invariant","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cat \u003e .tmp/canoncheck/cases4.go \u003c\u003c'EOF'\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\n\t\"github.com/punt-labs/beadle/internal/daemon\"\n)\n\nfunc collide() {\n\tvals := []string{\"X\", \"\\nX\", \"\\n\\nX\", \"\\n\\n\\nX\", \"X\\n\", \"X\\n\\n\", \"\\n\", \"\\n\\n\", \"\"}\n\tseen := map[string]string{}\n\tfor _, v := range vals {\n\t\tc := daemon.Command{Name: \"n\", Prompt: v}\n\t\tb, err := daemon.CanonicalCommandBytes(\u0026c)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Println(\"err\", err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif prev, ok := seen[string(b)]; ok {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"COLLISION: %q and %q produce identical canonical bytes\\n\", prev, v)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tseen[string(b)] = v\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println(\"collision probe done,\", len(seen), \"distinct encodings for\", len(vals), \"distinct prompts\")\n}\nEOF\nsed -i 's|^\\trunExtra3()|\\trunExtra3()\\n\\tcollide()|' .tmp/canoncheck/main.go \u0026\u0026 go run ./.tmp/canoncheck 2\u003e\u00261 | grep -E \"COLLISION|collision probe\""},"tool_input_hash":"1613d4bd6a618af81584d7c0fba54feb9f3fc6ee25983ad87f98f38a4f8c8901","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cat \\u003e .tmp/canoncheck/cases4.go \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\npackage main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/punt-labs/beadle/internal/daemon\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc collide() {\\n\\tvals := []string{..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:17:06.321492761Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \"$W\"; cat \u003e /tmp/pr-script.md \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nAdds `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` — drives `beadle-daemon`'s recipe tooling (`init`, `sign`, `verify`) end to end in a disposable sandbox, so the operator-facing path is checked repeatably instead of by hand.\n\n## Why\n\nbeadle's daemon recipes could not be authored at all until today (no signing tool, no `daemon.json`, an MCP registry that could not express the needed server). While verifying the tooling that fixes that, I ran the sequence by hand and **misread a failing command as passing** — I had piped it through `tail`, so `$?` was `tail`'s status. That is the class of mistake this script exists to prevent.\n\nCurrent run: **22 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.**\n\n## Reviewed adversarially, and it found a real own-goal\n\nThe operator's read of my first draft was \"those operations are not particularly safe.\" They were right. adb then reviewed it adversarially. The most important finding was mine to own:\n\n**The passphrase-leak assertion ran *after* the leak-prone diagnostic print.** Both failure branches printed the command's raw output, and only then checked whether that output contained the test passphrase. If `sign` ever actually leaked the passphrase, this script — the thing meant to *catch* that — would have put it on the terminal first. Now the leak flag is computed before any diagnostic, and the snippet is withheld entirely on detection rather than regex-redacted, because bash's `${var//pattern/repl}` treats the pattern as a glob and a real passphrase can contain glob metacharacters.\n\nOther findings fixed: `perl -pi -e` replaced with the repo's existing `sed_inplace()` helper (no new dependency, matches convention in `audit-install-shas.sh`); a real `usage()` function so `.bin/health/script-safety.py`'s `missing-help-handler` check passes (confirmed empirically before and after, not by reading the regex); `chmod 700` on the sandboxed `$HOME`, not just `$GNUPGHOME`, since the passphrase file lives under `$HOME`; and `run_check` no longer toggles `set +e`/`set -e` globally.\n\n## Four dangerous operations, one gate\n\n`rm -rf` in an EXIT trap, `gpgconf --kill gpg-agent`, recursive `chmod`, and reassigning `HOME` all route through `assert_sandbox`, which requires a non-empty path, the exact `mktemp` prefix, no `..`, not a symlink, and an existing directory.\n\nThe `gpgconf` one is the sharpest: with an unvalidated `GNUPGHOME`, `gpgconf` falls back to the **default** home and would kill the operator's real gpg-agent out from under other live sessions.\n\nadb tried and **could not build a working exploit** against the guards — `SANDBOX` only ever holds `mktemp`'s own output, and `/tmp` has the sticky bit set. The symlink check was added anyway as defense-in-depth, since the function is the shared gate for three destructive operations. It also verified directly that `TMPDIR` redirection does not move an explicit `/tmp/...` template on GNU or BSD `mktemp`.\n\n## Two judgment calls worth flagging\n\n**No `--apply` flag, deliberately.** `punt-kit/standards/shell.md` §Operational Safety requires scripts writing outside `.tmp/` to default to preview. This one does real work on bare invocation, with `--dry-run` as opt-in preview. Judged not to need it: every mutation is confined to a `mktemp` sandbox removed on exit, and nothing touches `~/.punt-labs/beadle`, the real GnuPG keyring, git, or GitHub — a materially different risk profile from the categories that rule targets. Precedent: `git-pull-all.sh` also mutates on bare invocation. Happy to add `--apply` if you would rather hold the line on the standard.\n\n**README safety class is `destructive (sandbox-scoped)`, not `read-only`.** It mints real GPG keys and runs the real subcommands; calling it read-only would mislead an operator reading the table.\n\n## Filed separately\n\n`punt-cnq` — `script-safety.py` does not flag this script for `destructive-without-apply-or-target`, but only by accident: `${2:?--repo needs a directory}` inside the *optional* `--repo` arm matches its required-positional regex. Right verdict, wrong route. Not fixed inline because that checker is shared and tightening it could newly flag existing scripts.\n\n## Verification\n\n`shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR` clean. `script-safety.py` zero violations. `--dry-run` works. Real run 22/0/0, sandbox cleaned up, nothing leaked into the beadle checkout.\nEOF\ngh pr create --repo punt-labs/punt-labs --base main --head chore/add-verify-recipe-path-script --title \"chore(.bin): add verify-recipe-path.sh for beadle recipe tooling\" --body-file /tmp/pr-script.md 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2","description":"Open the PR for the script"},"tool_input_hash":"fa4f6de840230edb8d0394d1f501671d46aff5f2c81beb2cbb724493d2e3f699","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \\\"$W\\\"; cat \\u003e /tmp/pr-script.md \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nAdds `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` — drives `beadle-daemon`'s recipe t..."}
