{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:17:41.405517657Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-code-08643c26562294d6","agent_type":"rev-code","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"grep -rn \"BinaryWhitelist{\" --include=*.go . | grep -v _test; echo \"=== validate ===\"; sed -n \"$(grep -n 'func validateCommand\\|func (c \\*Command) Validate' internal/daemon/command.go | head -1 | cut -d: -f1),+70p\" internal/daemon/command.go","description":"Find BinaryWhitelist construction and command validation"},"tool_input_hash":"b877216a99d1723db7b858925e986c3a0c4287b78271624d955d251cd13e3671","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"BinaryWhitelist{\\\" --include=*.go . | grep -v _test; echo \\\"=== validate ===\\\"; sed -n \\\"$(grep -n 'func validateCommand\\\\|func (c \\\\*Command) Validate' internal/daemon/command...."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:17:42.623423378Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Truncated mid-finding 2. **Send findings 2 throug…","message":"Truncated mid-finding 2. **Send findings 2 through 9** — do not repeat finding 1 or the \"what is correct\" section, both came through intact.\n\nBefore you do: finding 1 is accepted without argument and it is the most valuable thing anyone has produced on this branch. You did the one thing that catches it — you ran the actual transform on the actual file the README tells operators to sign, and pasted what `sign` would write. That is a category above reasoning about it.\n\nIt also exposes a hole in **my** harness, which I want you to know because it changes what I will ask for next. `.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh` asserts `signature written into the file` by grepping for `BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE`. That passes on a file whose comments have been deleted and whose zero values have been materialized. So my 22/22 was measuring \"a signature appeared,\" not \"the operator's recipe survived.\" A green harness that cannot see a destroyed source file is exactly the failure mode I have been warning others about all session, and I built one.\n\nTwo specifics I want in your remaining findings if you have not already covered them:\n\n- The `os.WriteFile` truncation point. You flagged it as compounding; I agree it is independently blocking. `punt-kit/standards/go.md` §8 mandates temp-plus-`os.Rename`, and `internal/daemon/persist.go` already does exactly that in this same package — so there is an in-repo pattern to copy, not just a standard to cite.\n- Whether the same re-marshal-over-source problem exists anywhere else in the diff, or is confined to `sign_cmd.go`.\n\nOn finding 2 (`docs-ask` answering from training data with `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` unset): send the rest of it. I want to know specifically whether the pipeline continues past `missingEnv` with only an Error log, and whether the worker's output is distinguishable downstream from a real documentation lookup. If a reply reaches the sender presenting model recall as a docs answer, that is worse than a failed stage and I will treat it as blocking regardless of how the log reads.\n\nKeep the same discipline for the rest: file:line, the concrete scenario, what an operator sees versus what happened, and blocking-versus-polish. Split across messages rather than truncating again.","recipient":"rev-silent","summary":"Send findings 2 onward — truncated","to":"rev-silent","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"0d4e2d156210783baf599467100d62dba6d24a80ef060c425fccee46bf57e98c","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Truncated mid-finding 2. **Send findings 2 throug…\",\"message\":\"Truncated mid-finding 2. **Send findings 2 through 9** — do not repeat finding 1 or the \\\"what is correct\\\" section, both..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:17:48.46312627Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-invariant-d1f64b9173a77bf7","agent_type":"rev-invariant","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"SB=$(mktemp -d /tmp/bg-XXXX)\nexport GNUPGHOME=\"$SB/g\"; mkdir -p \"$GNUPGHOME\"; chmod 700 \"$GNUPGHOME\"\ngpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase '' --quick-generate-key \"Good \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\" ed25519 sign 1y \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\ngpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase '' --quick-generate-key \"Never \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\" ed25519 sign never \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\ngpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase '' --quick-generate-key \"Other \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\" ed25519 sign 1y \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\nG=$(gpg --batch --with-colons -k [REDACTED:email] | awk -F: '/^fpr:/{print $10;exit}')\nN=$(gpg --batch --with-colons -k [REDACTED:email] | awk -F: '/^fpr:/{print $10;exit}')\nO=$(gpg --batch --with-colons -k [REDACTED:email] | awk -F: '/^fpr:/{print $10;exit}')\nD=\u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/beadle-daemon\nprintf 'name: t\\ndescription: d\\nrunner: cli\\nbinary: b\\noutput_schema: text\\n' \u003e \"$SB/r.yaml\"\ncp \"$SB/r.yaml\" \"$SB/unsigned.yaml\"\nset +e\necho \"--- missing (unsigned) ---\"; $D verify \"$SB/unsigned.yaml\" --signer \"$G\" 2\u003e\u00261 | head -1; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\n$D sign \"$SB/r.yaml\" --signer \"$G\" \u003e/dev/null; echo \"sign(good) exit=$?\"\necho \"--- good ---\"; $D verify \"$SB/r.yaml\" --signer \"$G\" 2\u003e\u00261|head -1; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\necho \"--- wrong-key ---\"; $D verify \"$SB/r.yaml\" --signer \"$O\" 2\u003e\u00261|head -1; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\ncp \"$SB/unsigned.yaml\" \"$SB/n.yaml\"\necho \"--- sign with non-expiring key ---\"; $D sign \"$SB/n.yaml\" --signer \"$N\" 2\u003e\u00261|head -2; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\necho \"--- file unchanged after failed sign? ---\"; diff -q \"$SB/n.yaml\" \"$SB/unsigned.yaml\" \u0026\u0026 echo SAME || echo CHANGED\necho \"--- invalid (tampered) ---\"; sed -i 's/description: d/description: e/' \"$SB/r.yaml\"; $D verify \"$SB/r.yaml\" --signer \"$G\" 2\u003e\u00261|head -1; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\""},"tool_input_hash":"2fa57faf5e6476f4ebfd80cdaa94786d344efc2502828c25306a3a38f3eaac33","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"SB=$(mktemp -d /tmp/bg-XXXX)\\nexport GNUPGHOME=\\\"$SB/g\\\"; mkdir -p \\\"$GNUPGHOME\\\"; chmod 700 \\\"$GNUPGHOME\\\"\\ngpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase '' --quick-generate-key \\\"Goo..."}
