{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:18:36.623527671Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \"$W\"; python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\np='.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"# Usage: verify-recipe-path.sh [--dry-run] [--repo DIR] [--keep]\",\n\"# Usage: verify-recipe-path.sh --apply [--repo DIR] [--keep]\", 1)\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"Usage: $(basename \"$0\") [--dry-run] [--repo DIR] [--keep]\n  --dry-run  Preview what would be exercised; mints no keys, runs no daemon.\n  --repo DIR beadle checkout to test (default: ~/Coding/punt-labs/beadle).\n  --keep     Leave the sandbox on disk after the run instead of deleting it\n             (it holds the two test GPG keys and the test passphrase file).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Usage: $(basename \"$0\") --apply [--repo DIR] [--keep]\n\nPreviews by default. Pass --apply to actually run.\n\n  --apply    Perform the run: mint GPG keys, execute init/sign/verify.\n             Required -- without it this only prints what would happen.\n  --repo DIR beadle checkout to test (default: ~/Coding/punt-labs/beadle).\n  --keep     Leave the sandbox on disk after the run instead of deleting it\n             (it holds the two test GPG keys and the test passphrase file).\"\"\", 1)\n\ns = s.replace(\"DRY_RUN=false\", \"APPLY=false\", 1)\ns = s.replace(\"    --dry-run) DRY_RUN=true; shift ;;\", \"    --apply)   APPLY=true; shift ;;\", 1)\ns = s.replace('if \"${DRY_RUN}\"; then', 'if ! \"${APPLY}\"; then', 1)\n\n# The header's safety-class note claimed sandbox confinement exempted it. It did not.\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"# Safety class: READ-ONLY with respect to the operator's real state.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"# Safety class: DESTRUCTIVE (sandbox-scoped). Previews by default; --apply is\n# required to do anything. punt-kit/standards/shell.md requires preview-by-\n# default for any script writing outside .tmp/, and this writes to\n# /tmp/bg-recipe-* -- being confined to a disposable directory is not an\n# exemption the standard grants, and \"safe because the author judged the\n# destination disposable\" is the self-assessment the rule exists to remove.\n# It also mints real GPG keys, reads a real secret from pass, and signals\n# gpg-agent -- that last one is not sandbox-shaped at all; its safety rests\n# entirely on assert_sandbox below.\n#\n# It is read-only with respect to the operator's persistent state:\"\"\", 1)\n\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('rewritten')\nPY\nsed -n '/^if ! \"\\${APPLY}\"/,/^fi$/p' .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh | head -14","description":"Make preview the default, require --apply"},"tool_input_hash":"404f1dc75561a6887b5145d069d4305cb5c763a17bc65fa7c8210f906256b7b7","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \\\"$W\\\"; python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'PY'\\np='.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh'\\ns=open(p).read()\\n\\ns = s.replace(\\n\\\"# Usage: verify-recip..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:18:48.345526864Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \"$W\"; python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\np='.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"  section 'Dry run: would exercise'\",\"  section 'Preview (no --apply): would exercise'\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"  printf '\\\\n  sandbox template: %s\\\\n  no changes made.\\\\n\\\\n' \\\"${SANDBOX_TEMPLATE}\\\"\",\n            \"  printf '\\\\n  sandbox template: %s\\\\n  no changes made. Re-run with --apply to execute.\\\\n\\\\n' \\\"${SANDBOX_TEMPLATE}\\\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\necho \"=== shellcheck ===\"; shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh \u0026\u0026 echo clean\necho \"=== bare invocation now previews ===\"; .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh --repo \u003crepo\u003e 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -5\necho \"=== safety checker ===\"; python3 .bin/health/script-safety.py .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo \"0 violations\" || echo \"see output\"","description":"Verify preview-by-default and shellcheck"},"tool_input_hash":"ba7bc442908212f12a1808a8eeca0f4fbdd189e5c2e3ad718f955756cfcb093a","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \\\"$W\\\"; python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'PY'\\np='.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh'\\ns=open(p).read()\\ns=s.replace(\\\"  section 'Dry run: would e..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:19:02.812755762Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-code-08643c26562294d6","agent_type":"rev-code","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"grep -rn \"cmd.Env\\|envOverrides\\|envMap\\|%v\\\", *env\\|passphrase\" --include=*.go internal/ cmd/ | grep -v _test.go","description":"Final sweep for env/passphrase stringification"},"tool_input_hash":"b232eb9a187f136aaeedf7dcd970e4a2bf0426e8594de6d52bca1d86fc72d7ce","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"cmd.Env\\\\|envOverrides\\\\|envMap\\\\|%v\\\\\\\", *env\\\\|passphrase\\\" --include=*.go internal/ cmd/ | grep -v _test.go\",\"description\":\"Final sweep for env/passphrase stringification\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:19:09.527143835Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","agent_id":"arev-silent-0b5e7e5e3c6716f9","agent_type":"rev-silent","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Findings 2-5 (BLOCKING). Finding 2 is confirmed w…","message":"Findings 2-5 (BLOCKING). Finding 2 is confirmed worse than I first wrote it: a reply DOES reach the sender presenting model recall as a docs answer, and there is zero validation on the path. Findings 6-9 plus your two specifics follow in my final message.\n\n## 2. `docs-ask` with `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` unset sends model recall to the sender as a documentation answer — BLOCKING\n\n`\u003crepo\u003e/internal/daemon/runner.go:60-73`\n\nYou asked whether the pipeline continues past `missingEnv` with only an Error log. It does — verbatim:\n\n```go\nenvOverrides, missingEnv := resolveEnvVars(cmd.EnvVars)\nfor _, name := range missingEnv {\n    e.Logger.Error(\"declared env var not set in daemon environment\",\n        \"pipeline\", p.ID, \"stage\", idx, \"command\", cmd.Name, \"var\", name)\n}\n\nwr, err := r.Spawner.Run(ctx, missionID, mcpPath, promptPath, envOverrides)\n```\n\nNo `return`, no status change, no marker threaded into the result. The loop logs and falls through to the spawn.\n\nYou also asked whether the output is distinguishable downstream from a real documentation lookup. **It is not, at four separate points, and I traced each one:**\n\n1. **The MCP failure is not an error to the worker process.** `templates.go:42` writes the literal `${CONTEXT7_API_KEY}` as the context7 header. Unset, Claude Code expands it to empty, context7 returns 401, and the session reports a *connection failure warning* — it does not abort. (This very session is proof of the mechanism: two of my own MCP servers failed to connect and I ran to completion.)\n2. **`IsError` stays false.** `spawner.go:209-212` sets `Output: parsed.Result, IsError: parsed.IsError` from the `claude --output-format json` envelope. A session that answered without a tool it wanted is not an error session, so `wr.IsError` is false and `runner.go:74` never fires.\n3. **`Output` is the final answer text only.** `parsed.Result` is the assistant's last message. Nothing in `WorkerResult` (`spawner.go:26-32`) records which MCP servers connected or which tools were called. The `Pipeline` record persisted to disk carries the same bare string.\n4. **Schema validation is a no-op for this recipe.** `docs-ask.yaml` declares `output_schema: text`. `CompileSchema` returns `(nil, nil)` for `\"text\"` (`schema.go:15-17`), and `ValidateOutput` returns nil immediately on a nil schema (`schema.go:33-35`). So the one gate that saves `sysreport` from finding 7 does not exist on this path at all.\n\n**Operator/sender sees:** a fluent, confident answer to a library-API question, delivered by email, indistinguishable in form from a context7-grounded one — and more likely to be *wrong* precisely for the fast-moving libraries the recipe exists to cover. **What happened:** the worker was told \"prefer context7's result over training-data recall,\" could not reach context7, and answered from recall anyway. The only trace is one `Error` line in `~/.punt-labs/beadle/logs/beadle-daemon.log` that nobody reads unless already suspicious — and by then the answer has been acted on.\n\nYour instinct is right: this is worse than a failed stage. A failed stage tells the sender nothing happened. This tells the sender something authoritative happened.\n\n**Recommendation** — fail the stage:\n\n```go\nif len(missingEnv) \u003e 0 {\n    return \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"command %q declares env var(s) %v, absent from the daemon's \"+\n        \"environment -- set them in the unit/plist that starts beadle-daemon; running \"+\n        \"without them would silently degrade this command\", cmd.Name, missingEnv)\n}\n```\n\n`fireElse` then replies to the sender with the real reason. A recipe that genuinely wants an optional var should declare it as one (`env_vars_optional:`), not get that behavior by default from every declaration. `envForCommand` (`runner.go:290-300`) has the identical log-and-continue shape for the `cli` runner and needs the same fix.\n\nNote the mechanism is pre-existing, but this branch is what makes it consequential — `docs-ask` is the first recipe whose declared env var is load-bearing for *answer correctness* rather than mere capability. I'd also drop `env_vars` from the recipe's contract entirely in favour of a `required_env` that the loader enforces, but that is a design call above this audit.\n\n## 3. \"round-trip verified\" does not mean \"the daemon will load this\" — BLOCKING\n\n`\u003crepo\u003e/cmd/beadle-daemon/sign_cmd.go:116`\n\nTwo independent ways to get a green `sign` and a daemon that refuses the file.\n\n**(a) `sign` never validates the command.** It decodes with `KnownFields(true)` and signs. It never calls `validateCommand` (`internal/daemon/command.go:161`). A recipe with `runner: cli` and no `binary`, an invalid `mode`, a missing `output_schema`, or an unparseable `timeout` signs cleanly, prints `round-trip verified`, and is rejected at daemon startup as `logger.Warn(\"skip invalid command file\", ...)` (`command.go:116`) — a Warn, in a log file, hours after the operator ran `sign`.\n\n**(b) `sign` never checks `--signer` against `daemon.json`.** Sign with any valid non-expiring key in your keyring and the round trip verifies, because `VerifySignature` is handed the same `--signer` value. The daemon verifies against `daemon.json`'s authorizer and logs `reason=wrong-key`. `verify` catches this, but only if run — and `sign`'s own success message is what tells the operator they don't need to.\n\n**Operator sees:** `signed sysreport.yaml (key ABC..., round-trip verified)`. **What happened:** a signature was proven self-consistent. Nothing about loadability was checked.\n\n**Recommendation.** Validate a *copy*, not the original: `validateCommand` mutates its argument (it defaults `Runner` and `Mode`, `command.go:166-174`), and `loadCommand` verifies the signature *before* validating (`command.go:142-156`), so the canonical bytes must stay pre-default. Signing post-default bytes would produce a file the daemon rejects — the exact failure you'd be trying to prevent.\n\n```go\nprobe := command // struct copy; validateCommand only writes scalar defaults\nif err := daemon.ValidateCommandShape(\u0026probe); err != nil {\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"%s is not a loadable command file, refusing to sign: %w\", path, err)\n}\n```\n\nThat needs a small exported wrapper over `validateCommand`. Separately, when `daemon.json` resolves, compare `--signer` to the authorizer and refuse on mismatch unless `--force`, naming both fingerprints. `resolveVerifySigner` (`verify_cmd.go:107`) is already exactly that helper — it just isn't called from `sign`.\n\n## 4. `init` writes `daemon.json` for a key that is not in the keyring — BLOCKING\n\n`\u003crepo\u003e/cmd/beadle-daemon/init_cmd.go:66-69`\n\n`ResolveOwnerKeyID` (`internal/daemon/config.go:48-80`) is pure syntax: exactly-one-field, ethos handle resolution, 40-hex regex. It never touches GPG.\n\n```\n$ beadle-daemon init --fingerprint 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567\nwrote [REDACTED:home-path].punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json (authorizer key 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567)\n```\n\n**Operator sees:** success — the file gating the entire zero-agent-authority invariant is now configured. **What happens:** every command file fails `ReasonInvalid: owner key ... not found in isolated keyring after import` (`signature.go:233-236`), or `ReasonKeyExpired` if the key is non-expiring — a hard invariant (`internal/pgp/expiry.go`) that most operator keys violate by default. The verdict arrives as a per-file `Error` at daemon startup, days later, at the far end of the pipeline from the typo.\n\nTo be clear about scope, since your brief asked the opposite question: `init` does **not** write a partial or empty file. The ordering at `init_cmd.go:60-91` is correct and the guard comment at `:53-59` is well reasoned. The gap is that the validation is too shallow for the confidence the success message projects.\n\n**Recommendation.** Probe the key before writing — both primitives are already exported and already used by `VerifySignature`:\n\n```go\nif err := pgp.CheckKeyExpiry(gpgBinary, resolvedFpr); err != nil {\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"authorizer key %s is not usable for signing: %w\\n\\n\"+\n        \"beadle-daemon requires a key present in this keyring whose expiration \"+\n        \"date has not passed\", resolvedFpr, err)\n}\n```\n\nAbsent-from-keyring surfaces through the same call. Add `--no-verify-key` for the deliberate configure-before-key-import case, so that escape hatch is explicit rather than the silent default.\n\n## 5. A locked `pass` store makes `sign` print the wrong remedy — MEDIUM\n\n`\u003crepo\u003e/internal/secret/secret.go:36`\n\n```go\nif val, err := keychainGet(name); err == nil \u0026\u0026 val != \"\" {\n    return val, nil\n}\n```\n\nEvery keychain-backend error is discarded — not logged, not wrapped — and resolution falls through to file, then env, then `ErrNotFound`.\n\nThe collapse you flagged in your brief is real, but it is here, not in the new code. `sign_cmd.go:90` handles the distinction correctly: `if err != nil \u0026\u0026 !errors.Is(err, secret.ErrNotFound)` returns, so an unsafe-permissions credential file does surface as `resolve signing passphrase: ...`. That part is right and I'd leave it alone.\n\n**Scenario:** the passphrase lives in `pass`, `gpg-agent` is not unlocked. `pass show` fails. `secret.Get` discards that and returns `ErrNotFound`. `sign` proceeds with `passphrase == \"\"`, gpg refuses, and `wrapSignError` (`sign_cmd.go:136-143`) prints *\"no passphrase was resolved for credential `gpg-passphrase` — if this key needs one, set it via the credential chain (OS keychain, or ~/.punt-labs/beadle/secrets/gpg-passphrase mode 600, or BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE).\"* They already did all of that. They will now spend an hour re-inserting a secret that is already correctly stored.\n\nThe message itself is genuinely good — it is the input that is wrong.\n\n**Recommendation.** Distinguish \"no entry in this backend\" from \"this backend is present and failed.\" Minimal version: thread the discarded error into `Get`'s final `ErrNotFound` wrap so the text reads `... not found (keychain: pass: gpg: decryption failed: No secret key; file; env BEADLE_GPG_PASSPHRASE)`. That one change turns a wrong remedy into the right one for every `secret.Get` caller, not just `sign`.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"Findings 2-5, blocking; docs-ask confirmed","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"03d8f47af94e8338e7e12ffb0002e3797320942c1f0a428682bbe96792e31a69","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Findings 2-5 (BLOCKING). Finding 2 is confirmed w…\",\"message\":\"Findings 2-5 (BLOCKING). Finding 2 is confirmed worse than I first wrote it: a reply DOES reach the sender presenting model..."}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T14:19:09.62984397Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \"$W\"; python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\nimport re\np='.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\n\n# Lift the preview block out of its current position (after preflight).\nm=re.search(r'\\nif ! \"\\$\\{APPLY\\}\"; then\\n.*?\\n  exit 0\\nfi\\n', s, re.S)\nassert m, 'preview block not found'\nblock=m.group(0)\ns=s[:m.start()]+'\\n'+s[m.end():]\n\nnew_block = '''\n# Preview runs before the preflight hard-fails: describing what would happen\n# must not require a built binary or a provisioned keyring.\nif ! \"${APPLY}\"; then\n  section 'Preview (no --apply): would exercise'\n  printf '  init          happy path, clobber refusal, --force\\\\n'\n  printf '  init          daemon.json names the key, permissions sane\\\\n'\n  printf '  sign          unsigned recipe -\u003e signed, round-trip reported\\\\n'\n  printf '  verify        valid / tampered / unsigned\\\\n'\n  printf '  sign          passphrase-protected key via gpg-passphrase\\\\n'\n  section 'Would require'\n  printf '  %-34s %s\\\\n' \"${REPO_DIR}/beadle-daemon\" \\\\\n    \"$([[ -x \"${REPO_DIR}/beadle-daemon\" ]] \u0026\u0026 echo present || echo 'MISSING (make build-daemon)')\"\n  printf '  %-34s %s\\\\n' 'gpg on PATH' \\\\\n    \"$(command -v gpg \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo present || echo MISSING)\"\n  printf '  %-34s %s\\\\n' \"pass ${PASS_ENTRY}\" \\\\\n    \"$(pass show \"${PASS_ENTRY}\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo readable || echo 'MISSING (pass insert)')\"\n  section 'Would mutate'\n  printf '  %s   (created, then deleted unless --keep)\\\\n' \"${SANDBOX_TEMPLATE}\"\n  printf '  HOME and GNUPGHOME redirected into it for the run\\\\n'\n  printf '\\\\n  no changes made. Re-run with --apply to execute.\\\\n\\\\n'\n  exit 0\nfi\n'''\n\nanchor = \"\\n# --- preflight\"\nassert anchor in s\ns = s.replace(anchor, new_block + anchor, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('preview lifted above preflight')\nPY\nshellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh \u0026\u0026 echo \"shellcheck clean\"; echo \"=== preview with no build ===\"; .bin/verify-recipe-path.sh --repo \u003crepo\u003e 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -14","description":"Lift preview above preflight and test"},"tool_input_hash":"830036eccb9289a085430554659452c471848ea1587de540a033d8d13d691c0c","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/adb-verify-recipe; cd \\\"$W\\\"; python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'PY'\\nimport re\\np='.bin/verify-recipe-path.sh'\\ns=open(p).read()\\n\\n# Lift the preview block out..."}
